 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "t": "Three questions people ask us about biomass.",
   "s": 9,
   "e": 81
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "t": "One. Can I sell biomass without a factory?",
   "s": 110,
   "e": 182
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "t": "Yes. Many people collect, bale and store crop residue, and supply pellet makers and plants. That is aggregation, a business on its own.",
   "s": 220,
   "e": 508
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "t": "Two. Why does the price change so much?",
   "s": 526,
   "e": 601
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "t": "Season, region, quality and distance. Straw is cheap at harvest and costly months later.",
   "s": 650,
   "e": 823
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "t": "Three. How do I find buyers outside my district?",
   "s": 842,
   "e": 946
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "t": "Today, mostly through contacts and calls. That is exactly the gap we are working on.",
   "s": 991,
   "e": 1143
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "t": "Have a question? Drop it in the comments.",
   "s": 1158,
   "e": 1232
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "t": "IndiaBiomass. Connecting India's biomass economy.",
   "s": 1258,
   "e": 1367
  }
 ],
